1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,804
Every company runs on processes, and on the guides that explain them.

2
00:00:04,954 --> 00:00:08,513
The day the software updates, those guides go out of date.

3
00:00:09,167 --> 00:00:14,190
Platforms like Dynamics 365 ship two release waves every year.

4
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:19,543
Each one sends training teams back to re-shoot, rewrite, and re-translate, by hand.

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:29,097
Gartner sized digital adoption at about a billion dollars in 2024, and SAP paid around one and a half billion for WalkMe.

6
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:35,137
The record-once incumbent, ClickLearn, made close to eight million euros in 2024,

7
00:00:35,187 --> 00:00:39,167
from more than eight hundred customers, with a Windows desktop client.

8
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:41,376
There is an opening, too.

9
00:00:41,426 --> 00:00:48,320
SAP's own training tool, Enable Now, takes no new cloud renewals after April 2027,

10
00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:50,604
so its customers need somewhere to go.

11
00:00:51,367 --> 00:00:57,885
Steplight does the same job from the browser, with no desktop client and no 16 GB workstation.

12
00:00:57,935 --> 00:01:00,449
Automated process testing is built in.

13
00:01:00,499 --> 00:01:02,872
The incumbent keeps it for its top tier.

14
00:01:03,733 --> 00:01:10,708
As an author clicks through a task, the browser extension describes each element several ways, most robust first:

15
00:01:11,167 --> 00:01:16,158
a stable ID, its role and name, its label, and its place on the page.

16
00:01:16,208 --> 00:01:19,604
It keeps only the ones that match exactly one element.

17
00:01:20,367 --> 00:01:23,009
Clicks and keystrokes collapse into clean steps.

18
00:01:23,059 --> 00:01:29,193
Each one gets its instruction written automatically, and sensitive values are masked in every output.

19
00:01:29,933 --> 00:01:33,670
Every step is stored as structured data, with its screenshot.

20
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:37,639
Resolve it for a language, and the same process feeds every output:

21
00:01:37,689 --> 00:01:40,881
documents, players, the portal, and live guidance.

22
00:01:41,733 --> 00:01:46,847
Replay drives the real application again in a headless browser, step by step.

23
00:01:46,897 --> 00:01:52,161
When an element has changed, Steplight finds it by the next selector, marks the step as healed,

24
00:01:52,211 --> 00:01:54,008
and refreshes the screenshot.

25
00:01:54,667 --> 00:01:59,466
Run it in test mode, and it becomes regression testing for business processes.

26
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:03,036
Localization uses the same engine.

27
00:02:03,086 --> 00:02:08,490
Replay runs the app in Danish or German, captures the real translated screens and labels,

28
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:12,931
and rebuilds every instruction from them, with no machine translation.

29
00:02:13,667 --> 00:02:15,678
Claude handles the language work.

30
00:02:15,728 --> 00:02:21,505
It answers learners' questions from your own documented processes, translates what authors write,

31
00:02:21,555 --> 00:02:25,622
and turns an existing Word guide into a draft you finish in the app.

32
00:02:25,672 --> 00:02:28,665
Without AI, everything still works offline.

33
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:33,296
Steplight ships as a single container on a dedicated server.

34
00:02:33,346 --> 00:02:39,844
Authoring sits behind an access key, analytics are anonymous, and the extension only talks to your own server.

35
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,110
All of this runs today.

36
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:51,164
About 140 automated tests, and a 39-check end-to-end run that records, replays, heals, translates, exports and publishes,

37
00:02:51,214 --> 00:02:52,845
pass on every change.

38
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,090
Next on the roadmap:

39
00:02:55,140 --> 00:03:01,676
one-click setup for whole organizations, hosting with backups, an Edge add-on listing, PDF import,

40
00:03:01,726 --> 00:03:03,992
and redaction inside the recorder.

41
00:03:05,133 --> 00:03:06,174
Steplight.

42
00:03:06,274 --> 00:03:10,698
Every process documented, trained and guided, and never out of date.
